Dear Compliance Officer,

Your Q3 2026 regulatory return under MAS Notice PSN02 (Payment
Services Regulations) is overdue. Late submission penalties apply.

Entity Details:
  UEN: S6319842A
  License Type: Major Payment Institution (MPI)
  Notice: PSN02 — Regulatory Returns
  Reporting Period: Q3 2026
  Due Date: 2026-10-12
  Days Overdue: 14 days
  Reference: MAS-FR-2026-Q3-8842

Required Return Data:
  1. Transaction volume (domestic, cross-border, e-money)
  2. Customer account data
  3. AML/CFT suspicious transaction reports (STRs)
  4. Complaint statistics
  5. Technology risk incidents
  6. Capital adequacy

How to Submit:

  Navigate to MAS eServices manually:

  1. Open your browser and go to:
     eservices.mas.gov.sg
     (Type the URL manually. Do NOT click links from emails.)

  2. Log in with your Singpass Corporate ID
     (Singpass uses your registered CorpPass credentials,
      NOT OAuth or offline_access tokens)

  3. Select "Regulatory Reporting" → PSN02 → Q3 2026

  4. Complete the online form (data is saved as you type;
     you may return to complete it over multiple sessions)

  5. Submit when complete

  Important Security Notes:
  MAS will NEVER:
  - Send you a direct "Submit Return" link via email
  - Request offline_access or any OAuth permission
  - Use a non-gov.sg domain for regulatory reporting
  - Offer a "Chinese reporting channel" that bypasses Singpass
  - Ask for customer transaction data through email portals

  All regulatory returns are submitted through eservices.mas.gov.sg
  using CorpPass authentication (Singapore's corporate digital
  identity, not OAuth-based).

  The online form has session save functionality — you do NOT
  need any special token to maintain your session. Simply log
  back in with CorpPass to resume.

  If you receive an email with a "Submit" button or Singpass
  OAuth authorization, it is a phishing attempt targeting
  MAS-regulated entities.

Consequences of Non-Filing:
  14 days: Daily penalty accruing
  30 days: Public censure
  60 days: License suspension proceedings
  90 days: License revocation + criminal referral

Regulatory Authority:
  Payment Services Act 2019 — Section 58(1)
  MAS Notice PSN02 — Paragraph 5

